i'm jennifer crumbly when james and  jennifer crumley appeared on a video  call to see their son in court on  wednesday they already knew they were  likely to face charges themselves  prosecutors say james crumley bought the  gun used by 15 year old ethan as a  christmas present his mother took him to  a gun range and laughed when he was  caught researching buying ammunition in  class  shortly before he opened fire teachers  found drawings on his desk depicting  scenes of a mass shooting his parents  were summoned but didn't take him home  reading this document looking at it  reading the words help me with a gun  blood everywhere this doesn't just have  impact me as a prosecutor and a lawyer  it impacts me as a mother  the notion  that a parent  could read those words and also know  that their son had access to a deadly  weapon  that they gave him  is unconscionable and i think it's  criminal the couple face a charge of  involuntary manslaughter for each of the  four teenagers who died that day  prosecutors say there's a mountain of  evidence that their son had been  planning the shooting for a long time  questions have also been raised about  whether the school should have done more  i believe mistakes were made at a number  of levels and  we're doing our best to you know make  sure that folks  that  were murdered on this tragic day get  justice  it's a measure of the nervousness in the  community that during a vigil for the  victims a panic broke out in the crowd  stay calm stay calm  stay  it calm out it was caused by someone  fainting  police say the crumblies will face  justice they'd even issued a warrant for  their arrest believing them to have gone  on the run it is highly unusual for the  parents of a suspect in a school  shooting to face charges like this but  as the prosecutor said america needs to  do better to prevent these tragedies in  her words enough is enough  greg milam sky news
 

